{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","hash":"c63ea8b37ac4bde65638dc4f0522e40b9077822c3a539eb854be8c78a9626422","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AUFtwx9pxMqygeFAh2yF6z","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35 && git add src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/OrcaHomeBackend.cpp src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/OrcaImport.cpp src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/OrcaImport.hpp tests/jusprin/test_orca_import.cpp && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nOrcaSlicer import: install each saved printer's base profile first, and keep the selection on Retry\n\nA fresh JusPrin loads a vendor's profiles only once one of its printers is\ninstalled, so every saved OrcaSlicer printer based on a Creality, Elegoo or\nQidi profile failed with \"its base profile isn't in JusPrin\". The import now\ninstalls each base JusPrin has a profile for before importing the files.\nSeen with a copy of Kenneth's OrcaSlicer folder: 3 of 8 printers failed\nbefore, all 8 import after.\n\nRetry re-ran \"select the first imported printer\" and moved the selection off\nOrcaSlicer's selected printer onto the retried one. It now keeps the earlier\nselection unless the retry itself brings OrcaSlicer's selected printer.\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
