{"parentUuid":"4e60fb45-81d2-4edc-bd45-7f8fdd94e9a2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c5616fa6-550f-4dd8-8c61-ee8df3eb5090","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A816P1sJHACdhfgdxdqEcU","type":"tool_result","content":"Nov  5 15:45:54 2026 /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35/build/arm64/src/RelWithDebInfo/OrcaSlicer.app/Contents/MacOS/OrcaSlicer\nNov  5 14:54:47 2026 /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35/build/arm64/src/RelWithDebInfo/OrcaSlicer.app/Contents/MacOS/jusprin-mcp\n?? .playwright-mcp/\n===== 2026-11-05T20:24:08.227Z\nNot everything is done. The server changes are pushed, but the app change and the staging deployment records are still only on this Mac. Production hasn't been rolled out at all.\n\n**Where each piece is:**\n\n- **JusPrin app:** branch `claude/elated-sutherland-84a741`, ending at 4b16e4b1eb. It's 19 commits ahead of `origin/jusprin-newui` and isn't pushed. The syndicate session asked the Moonraker test session to squash and merge it, but that hasn't happened: `jusprin-newui` doesn't contain it, locally or on GitHub.\n- **tsd-enterprise:** pushed. The syndicate work is one squashed commit, 1845fe74b9, on `origin/master` and on `origin/release`, favicon included. The unsquashed history is still on the local branch `claude/jusprin-syndicate`.\n- **obico-server:** pushed. JusPrin 2's own light theme and colors are f78ef6e8 on `origin/master`.\n- **ops:** not pushed. The local branch `claude/jusprin-host` has 8 commits: the jusprinv2 host, ingress and certificate, the syndicate set-up, and the staging releases obi.4072 and obi.4073. Staging already runs those changes, because they were applied with kubectl, but GitHub has no record of them.\n- **Production:** jusprinv2.obico.io doesn't respond yet. The Google settings, DNS and app record for it still need to be set up.\n\n**Testing against staging.** The build in the syndicate session's folder is current with its branch. This command starts it against staging with an empty data folder, so you see the first launch:\n\n```bash\nJUSPRIN_AGENT_ENDPOINT=https://jusprinv2-stg.obico.io/ent/jusprin/v2/responses /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/charming-chandrasekhar-21e920/build/arm64/src/RelWithDebInfo/OrcaSlicer.app/Contents/MacOS/OrcaSlicer --datadir ~/JusPrinStagingTest\n```\n\nI ran it once with a throwaway data folder and the app started normally, then I closed it. I didn't sign in, so I haven't seen it reach staging. Two things in the code say it will:\n\n- The app reads that variable before its built-in address.\n- The sign-in, pricing and password-reset addresses all come from it.\n\nTo start over from the first launch again, delete `~/JusPrinStagingTest` first.\n===== 2026-11-05T22:13:52.651Z\nThis runs the app from the main checkout, which I built at 12:42 from the latest jusprin-newui. It points the app at staging and starts it with an empty data folder, so you get the first launch from the Welcome screen:\n\n```bash\nrm -rf ~/JusPrinStagingTest && JUSPRIN_AGENT_ENDPOINT=https://jusprinv2-stg.obico.io/ent/jusprin/v2/responses /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/build/arm64/src/RelWithDebInfo/OrcaSlicer.app/Contents/MacOS/OrcaSlicer --datadir ~/JusPrinStagingTest\n```\n\nThe `rm -rf` clears the previous test run's data folder, so each launch starts the first-run flow from scratch. Right now that folder doesn't exist, and no other copy of the app is running.\n\nA few things to know:\n\n- Sign-in goes to jusprinv2-stg.obico.io in your system browser. Staging sends real emails, so for email sign-in use a `k+something@obico.io` address.\n- The app's Terminal output shows in the window you ran it from. Closing that terminal closes the app.\n- I've confirmed this command starts the app, but I haven't clicked through the first launch on this build myself.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4d570a31-0f82-4d9d-b106-a8c8c654c3e8","timestamp":"2026-11-06T0