{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:20:17.169Z","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","content":"<system-reminder>\nLinked sessions now (status, not an instruction): allauth-upgrade = local_2c0bf928-2175-4569-9108-2cb6cba1fb77 (idle); use-a-jusprin-syndicate = local_69a34677-cdae-4851-90bb-557cd0ba6d32 (idle); design-the-no-wizard-fir = local_e71c8b0a-6720-4250-85de-80d4899e6200 (working). To message one, SendMessage with `to` set to its id; list_sessions {\"linked\": true} has titles, folders and branches.\n</system-reminder>\n\n<cross-session-message from=\"local_e71c8b0a-6720-4250-85de-80d4899e6200\" from-name=\"Design the no-wizard first-run flow on the canvas\">\nNew piece of work: a File menu item that imports OrcaSlicer printers after the first launch. Build it after the first-run printer step.\n\nKenneth wrote this to the design session on 2026-11-05: \"I want to add a menu item under \"File\" to let user import orcaslicer profiles\". He also asked that it read \"Import from OrcaSlicer\", and said \"Yes, draw it\". The boards are orca-import-01 to 05 on the canvas, version 111. The spec has a new last section, \"File › Import › Import from OrcaSlicer… (after the first launch)\", in /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-printer-step-spec-2026-11-05.md (untracked, main checkout).\n\nIn short:\n- \"Import from OrcaSlicer…\" is the last item in File › Import, after OrcaSlicer's \"Import Configs…\". That code is in the import_menu block of MainFrame.cpp, an OrcaSlicer file, so add one line that calls fork code.\n- It opens a dialog over the current screen. The dialog uses the same detection, list and result as the first-launch screens 07 and 17, but without the first-launch parts: no signed-in line, no Start fresh, no Back.\n- The dialog has four states: printers found, imported, nothing new, and no folder found. Each has its own board.\n\nTwo details are proposed by the design session and not yet agreed by Kenneth. Build them as specified unless he says otherwise:\n- Printers JusPrin already has are listed as \"Already in JusPrin\" and skipped. Today plan_orca_import in Home/OrcaImport.cpp saves another \"… (Orca copy)\" of every preset whose name already exists, so a second run from the menu would double every printer, filament and process. \"Already in JusPrin\" means a preset with the same name and the same inherits.\n- An import from the menu doesn't change the open project's printer. The first launch still selects one, as it does today.\n\nProof I'd like back:\n- Run the menu import twice against a copy of an OrcaSlicer folder.\n- After the second run, show that the dialog shows the \"nothing new\" state and that JusPrin's user preset folder has no \"(Orca copy)\" files.\n- Show the no-folder state with a scratch datadir that has no OrcaSlicer folder next to it.\n</cross-session-message>"}
