n and not yet agreed by Kenneth. Build them as specified unless he says otherwise:\n- Printers JusPrin already has are listed as \"Already in JusPrin\" and skipped. Today plan_orca_import in Home/OrcaImport.cpp saves another \"… (Orca copy)\" of every preset whose name already exists, so a second run from the menu would double every printer, filament and process. \"Already in JusPrin\" means a preset with the same name and the same inherits.\n- An import from the menu doesn't change the open project's printer. The first launch still selects one, as it does today.\n\nProof I'd like back:\n- Run the menu import twice against a copy of an OrcaSlicer folder.\n- After the second run, show that the dialog shows the \"nothing new\" state and that JusPrin's user preset folder has no \"(Orca copy)\" files.\n- Show the no-folder state with a scratch datadir that has no OrcaSlicer folder next to it.\n</cross-session-message>"},"uuid":"f4552ed9-e2d7-4bb0-b4e9-2f0c194d81f1","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:20:17.208Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","promptSource":"sdk","turnOrigin":"sdk","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":57,"turnIndex":85},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/first-run-printer-step","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
