{"parentUuid":"54e1860a-fb88-4a19-9145-9c942bb3ca5c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4fcc31c2-3e80-420b-a5c6-f7cbf63689ec","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XVJFoWAbUv5z7NvkfEfhBe","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# First launch: the printer step and the skipped-printer Home card\n9:## Why the built screens confuse\n15:## Board 08: \"Which printer do you have?\" (replaces the dialog on the Printers step)\n36:## Board 07: the same carried-over line as 08\n40:## Board 07: find the printers ticked in OrcaSlicer, not only the saved ones\n59:## Board 17: \"Imported from OrcaSlicer\"\n63:## Board 10: Home after \"Skip for now\"\n73:## Connecting a printer on Home\n77:## The printer chip in a project (agreed by Kenneth, 2026-11-05)\n81:## Board 09\n85:## File › Import › Import from OrcaSlicer… (after the first launch)\n## File › Import › Import from OrcaSlicer… (after the first launch)\n\nKenneth, 2026-11-05: \"I want to add a menu item under \"File\" to let user import orcaslicer profiles\", the item reading \"Import from OrcaSlicer\", and \"Yes, draw it\". Boards `orca-import-01` to `05` on the canvas (version 111), in the row \"Later, from the File menu\" under Home.\n\n- **01. The menu item.** \"Import from OrcaSlicer…\" is the last item in File › Import, after OrcaSlicer's own \"Import Configs…\" (`MainFrame.cpp`, the `import_menu` block). MainFrame.cpp is an OrcaSlicer file, so add one `append_menu_item` line that calls into fork code, and follow `fork-stewardship.md`.\n- **02. The dialog,** over whatever screen is open. It has a title row \"Import from OrcaSlicer\" with a close button. The lead says \"JusPrin found 2 printers in OrcaSlicer that it doesn't have yet. JusPrin copies them with their filaments, settings and printer connections. OrcaSlicer keeps its own copy.\" Below that is the same list as 07, then the folder path with \"Choose another folder…\". The buttons are Cancel and \"Import N printers\". It uses the same detection as 07, including ticked and selected printers. It has none of the first-launch parts: no carried line, no Start fresh, no Back.\n- **03. The result.** Title \"Imported from OrcaSlicer\", then \"They are in the printer menu. The printer this project uses didn't change. OrcaSlicer's own files were not changed.\" Below that are the same lines as 17 and the filament count, then Done.\n- **04. Nothing new.** Every printer is listed as \"Already in JusPrin\". The lead says \"Every printer in this OrcaSlicer folder is already in JusPrin, so there is nothing to import.\" The only buttons are \"Choose another folder…\" and Close.\n- **05. No folder found.** \"JusPrin didn't find OrcaSlicer's folder on this computer. If OrcaSlicer keeps its settings somewhere else, choose that folder.\" It shows the path it looked in, with Cancel and \"Choose the folder…\".\n\nProposed by the design session, not yet agreed by Kenneth:\n- Printers JusPrin already has show as \"Already in JusPrin\" and are skipped, along with their filaments and processes. Today `plan_orca_import` (`Home/OrcaImport.cpp`) saves a second copy, \"… (Orca copy)\", of any preset whose name JusPrin already has, so a second run would double everything. A preset counts as \"already in JusPrin\" when JusPrin has a preset with the same name and the same `inherits`. A same-named preset with different settings still imports as \"(Orca copy)\", as today.\n- The import from the menu doesn't change the open project's printer. It only adds printers to the printer menu. The first launch still selects one, as it does today.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cb4d620d-83e4-4b8d-be1d-276735706749","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:20:47.144Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"1:# First launch: the printer step and the skipped-printer Home card\n9:## Why the built screens confuse\n15:## Board 08: \"Which printer do you have?\" (replaces the dialog on the Printers step)\n36:## Board 07: the same carried-over line as 08\n40:## Board 07: find the printers ticked in OrcaSlicer, not only the saved ones\n59:## Board 17: \"Imported from OrcaSlicer\"\n63:## Board 10: Home after \"Skip for now\"\n73:## Connecting a printer on Home\n77:## The printer chip in a project (agreed by Kenneth, 2026-11-05)\n81:## Board 09\n85:## File › Import › Import from OrcaSlicer… (after the first launch)\n## File › Import › Import from OrcaSlicer… (after the first launch)\n\nKenneth, 2026-11-05: \"I want to add a menu item under \"File\" to let user import orcaslicer profiles\", the item reading \"Import from OrcaSlicer\", and \"Yes, draw it\". Boards `orca-import-01` to `05` on the canvas (version 111), in the row \"Later, from the File menu\" under Home.\n\n- **01. The menu item.** \"Import from OrcaSlicer…\" is the last item in File › Import, after OrcaSlicer's own \"Import Configs…\" (`MainFrame.cpp`, the `import_menu` block). MainFrame.cpp is an OrcaSlicer file, so add one `append_menu_item` line that calls into fork code, and follow `fork-stewardship.md`.\n- **02. The dialog,** over whatever screen is open. It has a title row \"Import from OrcaSlicer\" with a close button. The lead says \"JusPrin found 2 printers in OrcaSlicer that it doesn't have yet. JusPrin copies them with their filaments, settings and printer connections. OrcaSlicer keeps its own copy.\" Below that is the same list as 07, then the folder path with \"Choose another folder…\". The buttons are Cancel and \"Import N printers\". It uses the same detection as 07, including ticked and selected printers. It has none of the first-launch parts: no carried line, no Start fresh, no Back.\n- **03. The result.** Title \"Imported from OrcaSlicer\", then \"They are in the printer menu. The printer this project uses didn't change. OrcaSlicer's own files were not changed.\" Below that are the same lines as 17 and the filament count, then Done.\n- **04. Nothing new.** Every printer is listed as \"Already in JusPrin\". The lead says \"Every printer in this OrcaSlicer folder is already in JusPrin, so there is nothing to import.\" The only buttons are \"Choose another folder…\" and Close.\n- **05. No folder found.** \"JusPrin didn't find OrcaSlicer's folder on this computer. If OrcaSlicer keeps its settings somewhere else, choose that folder.\" It shows the path it looked in, with Cancel and \"Choose the folder…\".\n\nProposed by the design session, not yet agreed by Kenneth:\n- Printers JusPrin already has show as \"Already in JusPrin\" and are skipped, along with their filaments and processes. Today `plan_orca_import` (`Home/OrcaImport.cpp`) saves a second copy, \"… (Orca copy)\", of any preset whose name JusPrin already has, so a second run would double everything. A preset counts as \"already in JusPrin\" when JusPrin has a preset with the same name and the same `inherits`. A same-named preset with different settings still imports as \"(Orca copy)\", as today.\n- The import from the menu doesn't change the open project's printer. It only adds printers to the printer menu. The first launch still selects one, as it does today.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"54e1860a-fb88-4a19-9145-9c942bb3ca5c","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/first-run-printer-step","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
