{"parentUuid":"1e6b9b83-d39a-4ba2-bf36-dab384014aa7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4fcc31c2-3e80-420b-a5c6-f7cbf63689ec","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TjFJk9ovMjDPoLNXAhJ4Wi","type":"tool_result","content":"Home:\nHomeBackend.hpp\nHomeHost.cpp\nHomeHost.hpp\nHomeSnapshot.cpp\nHomeSnapshot.hpp\nHomeWebView.cpp\nHomeWebView.hpp\nMonitorWindow.cpp\nMonitorWindow.hpp\nOnboardingModel.cpp\nOnboardingModel.hpp\nOrcaHomeBackend.cpp\nOrcaHomeBackend.hpp\nOrcaImport.cpp\nOrcaImport.hpp\nPopOutWindow.cpp\nPopOutWindow.hpp\nPrintHistory.cpp\nPrintHistory.hpp\nPrinterWindow.cpp\nPrinterWindow.hpp\nProjectStatus.cpp\nProjectStatus.hpp\n\nHomeUI/src:\nApp.test.tsx\nApp.tsx\nbridge\ncomponents\nhistory.test.ts\nhistory.ts\nmain.tsx\nsavedDate.test.ts\nsavedDate.ts\nstate\nstyles.css\nstyles.test.ts\ntest\ntokens.ts\n\nHomeUI/src/components:\nAgentGroup.tsx\nCodeField.tsx\nConfirmDialog.tsx\nGlyphs.tsx\nOnboarding.tsx\nPrintHistory.tsx\nPrintReportForm.tsx\nPrinterCard.test.tsx\nPrinterCard.tsx\nPrinterMenu.tsx\nPrinterPickerHost.tsx\nProjectCard.tsx\n    1804 Home/OrcaHomeBackend.cpp\n     342 Home/OrcaImport.cpp\n     133 Home/OrcaImport.hpp\n     536 HomeUI/src/components/Onboarding.tsx\n    2815 total\n---\nname: agent-setup-embedded-in-printer-dialog\ndescription: \"Implemented (2026-09-13): 'Set up the agent' inside Add a printer now embeds the setup flow via a second AgentWebView instead of redirecting; chromeless rendering via ?embedded=1; a WebKit XPC flake to watch for in future manual testing\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 39ab79c2-8166-4a6c-aab4-90964465ffbd\n  modified: 2026-09-14T02:10:01.854Z\n---\n\nImplemented the design from [[add-printer-flow-figma-discrepancy]]'s follow-up\ndiscussion: `PrinterSetupDialog`'s \"Set up the agent\" button no longer closes\nthe modal and redirects to the docked Agent panel. It now builds a second,\nthrowaway `AgentWebView` (own `AgentService`/`AgentSetupService`, no\n`start_mcp()` call) and embeds it directly in the dialog.\n\n**Key pieces, for the next session touching this:**\n- `PrinterSetupDialog::set_up_agent()` lazily builds `m_setup_webview` via an\n  injected `MakeSetupWebViewFn` factory, calls `host().request_setup()` to\n  open straight to `SetupChooser`, and rebuilds. A completion callback\n  (`AgentHost::set_setup_completed_listener`, new — didn't exist before)\n  fires once `pump_setup()` successfully installs the verified agent; it sets\n  `m_agent_connected = true` and `CallAfter`s the teardown (destroying the\n  webview from a callback invoked by that same webview's own host would be\n  use-after-free otherwise).\n- `rebuild()` must detach `m_setup_webview` from its sizer *before*\n  `m_root->Clear(true)` on every call (including DPI-change rebuilds), since\n  `Clear(true)` destroys sizer children.\n- Docked-panel staleness fix: `ShellController::mark_agent_config_possibly_changed()`\n  sets a flag consumed by `on_page_changed()` (the same hook already used for\n  `m_home->refresh()`), which re-derives availability via\n  `Agent::load_agent_runtime()` and pushes it into the docked pane's\n  `AgentHost::set_agent()` — not a full webview reload.\n- **Chrome-stripping fix (added after initial implementation, per Kenneth's\n  live feedback):** the embedded webview initially showed the full chat page\n  shell (ChatHeader \"New chat\" title, +, ... buttons) around the setup card,\n  because it loads the exact same `index.html`/`App.tsx` as the docked panel.\n  Fixed with a new `AppProps.embedded` prop (read from `?embedded=1` in the\n  page URL, set by `AgentWebView`'s new `embedded` ctor param) that makes\n  `App.tsx` early-return just `{errorNotice}` + `body()`, skipping","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c5226bbc-5a2b-4bb3-944c-6a0c328efc8c","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:21:20.869Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Home:\nHomeBackend.hpp\nHomeHost.cpp\nHomeHost.hpp\nHomeSnapshot.cpp\nHomeSnapshot.hpp\nHomeWebView.cpp\nHomeWebView.hpp\nMonitorWindow.cpp\nMonitorWindow.hpp\nOnboardingModel.cpp\nOnboardingModel.hpp\nOrcaHomeBackend.cpp\nOrcaHomeBackend.hpp\nOrcaImport.cpp\nOrcaImport.hpp\nPopOutWindow.cpp\nPopOutWindow.hpp\nPrintHistory.cpp\nPrintHistory.hpp\nPrinterWindow.cpp\nPrinterWindow.hpp\nProjectStatus.cpp\nProjectStatus.hpp\n\nHomeUI/src:\nApp.test.tsx\nApp.tsx\nbridge\ncomponents\nhistory.test.ts\nhistory.ts\nmain.tsx\nsavedDate.test.ts\nsavedDate.ts\nstate\nstyles.css\nstyles.test.ts\ntest\ntokens.ts\n\nHomeUI/src/components:\nAgentGroup.tsx\nCodeField.tsx\nConfirmDialog.tsx\nGlyphs.tsx\nOnboarding.tsx\nPrintHistory.tsx\nPrintReportForm.tsx\nPrinterCard.test.tsx\nPrinterCard.tsx\nPrinterMenu.tsx\nPrinterPickerHost.tsx\nProjectCard.tsx\n    1804 Home/OrcaHomeBackend.cpp\n     342 Home/OrcaImport.cpp\n     133 Home/OrcaImport.hpp\n     536 HomeUI/src/components/Onboarding.tsx\n    2815 total\n---\nname: agent-setup-embedded-in-printer-dialog\ndescription: \"Implemented (2026-09-13): 'Set up the agent' inside Add a printer now embeds the setup flow via a second AgentWebView instead of redirecting; chromeless rendering via ?embedded=1; a WebKit XPC flake to watch for in future manual testing\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 39ab79c2-8166-4a6c-aab4-90964465ffbd\n  modified: 2026-09-14T02:10:01.854Z\n---\n\nImplemented the design from [[add-printer-flow-figma-discrepancy]]'s follow-up\ndiscussion: `PrinterSetupDialog`'s \"Set up the agent\" button no longer closes\nthe modal and redirects to the docked Agent panel. It now builds a second,\nthrowaway `AgentWebView` (own `AgentService`/`AgentSetupService`, no\n`start_mcp()` call) and embeds it directly in the dialog.\n\n**Key pieces, for the next session touching this:**\n- `PrinterSetupDialog::set_up_agent()` lazily builds `m_setup_webview` via an\n  injected `MakeSetupWebViewFn` factory, calls `host().request_setup()` to\n  open straight to `SetupChooser`, and rebuilds. A completion callback\n  (`AgentHost::set_setup_completed_listener`, new — didn't exist before)\n  fires once `pump_setup()` successfully installs the verified agent; it sets\n  `m_agent_connected = true` and `CallAfter`s the teardown (destroying the\n  webview from a callback invoked by that same webview's own host would be\n  use-after-free otherwise).\n- `rebuild()` must detach `m_setup_webview` from its sizer *before*\n  `m_root->Clear(true)` on every call (including DPI-change rebuilds), since\n  `Clear(true)` destroys sizer children.\n- Docked-panel staleness fix: `ShellController::mark_agent_config_possibly_changed()`\n  sets a flag consumed by `on_page_changed()` (the same hook already used for\n  `m_home->refresh()`), which re-derives availability via\n  `Agent::load_agent_runtime()` and pushes it into the docked pane's\n  `AgentHost::set_agent()` — not a full webview reload.\n- **Chrome-stripping fix (added after initial implementation, per Kenneth's\n  live feedback):** the embedded webview initially showed the full chat page\n  shell (ChatHeader \"New chat\" title, +, ... buttons) around the setup card,\n  because it loads the exact same `index.html`/`App.tsx` as the docked panel.\n  Fixed with a new `AppProps.embedded` prop (read from `?embedded=1` in the\n  page URL, set by `AgentWebView`'s new `embedded` ctor param) that makes\n  `App.tsx` early-return just `{errorNotice}` + `body()`, skipping","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1e6b9b83-d39a-4ba2-bf36-dab384014aa7","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/first-run-printer-step","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
