{"parentUuid":"785f6ebf-5b5b-4198-bd99-4d74e3f8640c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4fcc31c2-3e80-420b-a5c6-f7cbf63689ec","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NEtT3MjhtyPWoVCrZCsmtw","type":"tool_result","content":"462:.jp-icon-printer { -webkit-mask-image: url('@resources/jusprin/ui/icons/printer.svg'); mask-image: url('@resources/jusprin/ui/icons/printer.svg'); }\n463:.jp-icon-circle-check { -webkit-mask-image: url('@resources/jusprin/ui/icons/circle-check.svg'); mask-image: url('@resources/jusprin/ui/icons/circle-check.svg'); }\n467:.jp-icon-check { -webkit-mask-image: url('@resources/jusprin/ui/icons/check.svg'); mask-image: url('@resources/jusprin/ui/icons/check.svg'); }\n473:.jp-icon-triangle-alert { -webkit-mask-image: url('@resources/jusprin/ui/icons/triangle-alert.svg'); mask-image: url('@resources/jusprin/ui/icons/triangle-alert.svg'); }\n1508:button.primary {\n1517:button.primary:hover:enabled {\n1522:button.primary:active:enabled {\n1527:button.primary:disabled {\n2472:button.primary.wide {\n4416:.app--welcome {\n4420:.welcome {\n4430:.welcome-card {\n4443:.welcome-head,\n4444:.welcome-list {\n4450:.welcome-eyebrow {\n4455:.welcome-title {\n4467:.welcome-account {\n4476:.welcome-offer {\n4482:.welcome-account-line,\n4483:.welcome-row {\n4489:.welcome-account-title {\n4494:.welcome-account-action {\n4505:.welcome-row {\n4514:.welcome-row-copy {\n4521:.welcome-row-title {\n4526:.welcome-row-detail,\n4527:.welcome-row-count {\n4532:.welcome-row-count {\n4536:.welcome-icon--done {\n4540:.welcome-icon--warning {\n4544:.welcome-continue {\n  type: project\n---\n\n`src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/styles.css` is one flat global stylesheet\nwith no CSS modules or scoping. The `setup-*` prefix is already taken by the\nagent **setup screens** (`Setup.tsx`, `SetupLocalTool.tsx`) — `.setup-card`\nthere is `display: flex; flex-direction: column` on a lavender\n`--surface-selected` ground.\n\n**Why:** a new component that reuses one of those names silently inherits\n`display: flex` and leaks its own rules back onto the setup screens. This cost\nreal time once: the \"Current setup\" card reused `.setup-card`, which defeated\nits `white-space: nowrap` title clamp and re-tinted its background. Both\nsuites stayed green — jsdom does no layout, so no unit test can see it.\n\n**How to apply:** pick a prefix that does not already appear in styles.css","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"70f1dbf2-955b-4310-a131-bf421334e88a","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:34:19.299Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"462:.jp-icon-printer { -webkit-mask-image: url('@resources/jusprin/ui/icons/printer.svg'); mask-image: url('@resources/jusprin/ui/icons/printer.svg'); }\n463:.jp-icon-circle-check { -webkit-mask-image: url('@resources/jusprin/ui/icons/circle-check.svg'); mask-image: url('@resources/jusprin/ui/icons/circle-check.svg'); }\n467:.jp-icon-check { -webkit-mask-image: url('@resources/jusprin/ui/icons/check.svg'); mask-image: url('@resources/jusprin/ui/icons/check.svg'); }\n473:.jp-icon-triangle-alert { -webkit-mask-image: url('@resources/jusprin/ui/icons/triangle-alert.svg'); mask-image: url('@resources/jusprin/ui/icons/triangle-alert.svg'); }\n1508:button.primary {\n1517:button.primary:hover:enabled {\n1522:button.primary:active:enabled {\n1527:button.primary:disabled {\n2472:button.primary.wide {\n4416:.app--welcome {\n4420:.welcome {\n4430:.welcome-card {\n4443:.welcome-head,\n4444:.welcome-list {\n4450:.welcome-eyebrow {\n4455:.welcome-title {\n4467:.welcome-account {\n4476:.welcome-offer {\n4482:.welcome-account-line,\n4483:.welcome-row {\n4489:.welcome-account-title {\n4494:.welcome-account-action {\n4505:.welcome-row {\n4514:.welcome-row-copy {\n4521:.welcome-row-title {\n4526:.welcome-row-detail,\n4527:.welcome-row-count {\n4532:.welcome-row-count {\n4536:.welcome-icon--done {\n4540:.welcome-icon--warning {\n4544:.welcome-continue {\n  type: project\n---\n\n`src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src/styles.css` is one flat global stylesheet\nwith no CSS modules or scoping. The `setup-*` prefix is already taken by the\nagent **setup screens** (`Setup.tsx`, `SetupLocalTool.tsx`) — `.setup-card`\nthere is `display: flex; flex-direction: column` on a lavender\n`--surface-selected` ground.\n\n**Why:** a new component that reuses one of those names silently inherits\n`display: flex` and leaks its own rules back onto the setup screens. This cost\nreal time once: the \"Current setup\" card reused `.setup-card`, which defeated\nits `white-space: nowrap` title clamp and re-tinted its background. Both\nsuites stayed green — jsdom does no layout, so no unit test can see it.\n\n**How to apply:** pick a prefix that does not already appear in styles.css","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"785f6ebf-5b5b-4198-bd99-4d74e3f8640c","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/AgentUI/src","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/orca-import-menu","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
