{"parentUuid":"5057bc3c-2c10-4aad-a774-8b93127912d8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkssHasCwbeTsh7kz8JP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The diff matches what was built and tested, and the only change to OrcaSlicer's own code is the one menu line in MainFrame.cpp. Committing everything except the untracked `.playwright-mcp/` folder."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5547,"cache_read_input_tokens":275730,"output_tokens":1218,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":121},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5547,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1218,"cache_read_input_tokens":275730,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5547,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5547},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgkssHKFT4uxXw522HQWo","requestRef":"9c3bd8be-0da9-408d-b188-8e11285dbabe","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"update_plan","type":"assistant","uuid":"b221b4d4-8151-48c5-bf76-7a5bd5e44d2c","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:22:31.646Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/orca-import-menu","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
{"parentUuid":"b221b4d4-8151-48c5-bf76-7a5bd5e44d2c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkssHasCwbeTsh7kz8JP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TmqvXoLdDyQVd2pGTWz4ai","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add resources/jusprin/ui/design-tokens.json src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin tests/brand/test_brand_tokens.cpp tests/jusprin/test_orca_import.cpp src/slic3r/GUI/MainFrame.cpp && git status --short | grep -v \"^M \\|^A \" ; git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nFile › Import › Import from OrcaSlicer: bring OrcaSlicer's printers in later, skipping what JusPrin already has\n\nA new last item in File › Import opens a window over the current screen.\nIt finds OrcaSlicer's folder the way the first launch's Printers step\ndoes, lists its printers, and marks each one JusPrin already has as\n\"Already in JusPrin\". The window has five screens: found, imported,\nnothing new, no folder, and a picked folder that holds no printers.\n\nWhat it imports:\n- A preset counts as already in JusPrin when JusPrin has one with the\n  same name, or a renamed \"(Orca copy)\" of it, that inherits the same\n  base. The base is compared as JusPrin loads it: OrcaSlicer falls back\n  from a missing \"Elegoo Generic ABS\" to \"Generic ABS @System\", and the\n  imported copy is saved inheriting that. Without this, a second import\n  saved such a filament again as \"(Orca copy)\".\n- The open project's printer, filaments and process stay selected. The\n  one exception is the generic printer the first launch installs when the\n  person names none: it gives way to the imported printers, as on the\n  first launch, and the result names the printer now in use.\n- Installing a printer profile reloads every preset, so OrcaSlicer's own\n  save-or-discard prompt runs first when unsaved preset edits exist.\n\nThe first launch and the menu share one importer: OrcaImporter, moved\nout of OrcaHomeBackend.\n\nRebase note for MainFrame.cpp (OrcaSlicer-owned): one additive\nappend_menu_item call in init_menubar_as_editor, in the import_menu\nblock right after \"Import Configs\". It calls\nJusPrin::installed_shell()->open_orca_import() and is enabled only when\nthe shell is installed. Carry it there at each rebase.\n\nTested: jusprin_tests (166 cases), brand_tokens_tests, shell_theme_tests,\nAgentUI vitest (674). In the built app on a copy of an OrcaSlicer folder:\nfirst import brought 8 printers and 3 filaments; second showed \"nothing\nnew\" with no \"(Orca copy)\" files; a third with one added printer imported\nonly it and kept the project's printer; a data folder with no OrcaSlicer\nfolder beside it showed the no-folder screen.\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Commit the menu import work"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5547,"cache_read_input_tokens":275730,"output_tokens":1218,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":121},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5547,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1218,"cache_read_input_tokens":275730,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5547,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5547},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01TmqvXoLdDyQVd2pGTWz4ai":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35 && git add resources/jusprin/ui/design-tokens.json src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin tests/brand/test_brand_tokens.cpp tests/jusprin/test_orca_import.cpp src/slic3r/GUI/MainFrame.cpp && git status --short | grep -v \"^M \\|^A \" ; git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nFile › Import › Import from OrcaSlicer: bring OrcaSlicer's printers in later, skipping what JusPrin already has\n\nA new last item in File › Import opens a window over the current screen.\nIt finds OrcaSlicer's folder the way the first launch's Printers step\ndoes, lists its printers, and marks each one JusPrin already has as\n\"Already in JusPrin\". The window has five screens: found, imported,\nnothing new, no folder, and a picked folder that holds no printers.\n\nWhat it imports:\n- A preset counts as already in JusPrin when JusPrin has one with the\n  same name, or a renamed \"(Orca copy)\" of it, that inherits the same\n  base. The base is compared as JusPrin loads it: OrcaSlicer falls back\n  from a missing \"Elegoo Generic ABS\" to \"Generic ABS @System\", and the\n  imported copy is saved inheriting that. Without this, a second import\n  saved such a filament again as \"(Orca copy)\".\n- The open project's printer, filaments and process stay selected. The\n  one exception is the generic printer the first launch installs when the\n  person names none: it gives way to the imported printers, as on the\n  first launch, and the result names the printer now in use.\n- Installing a printer profile reloads every preset, so OrcaSlicer's own\n  save-or-discard prompt runs first when unsaved preset edits exist.\n\nThe first launch and the menu share one importer: OrcaImporter, moved\nout of OrcaHomeBackend.\n\nRebase note for MainFrame.cpp (OrcaSlicer-owned): one additive\nappend_menu_item call in init_menubar_as_editor, in the import_menu\nblock right after \"Import Configs\". It calls\nJusPrin::installed_shell()->open_orca_import() and is enabled only when\nthe shell is installed. Carry it there at each rebase.\n\nTested: jusprin_tests (166 cases), brand_tokens_tests, shell_theme_tests,\nAgentUI vitest (674). In the built app on a copy of an OrcaSlicer folder:\nfirst import brought 8 printers and 3 filaments; second showed \"nothing\nnew\" with no \"(Orca copy)\" files; a third with one added printer imported\nonly it and kept the project's printer; a data folder with no OrcaSlicer\nfolder beside it showed the no-folder screen.\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Commit the menu import work"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01TmqvXoLdDyQVd2pGTWz4ai":{"cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgkssHKFT4uxXw522HQWo","requestRef":"9c3bd8be-0da9-408d-b188-8e11285dbabe","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"update_plan","type":"assistant","uuid":"618c2d58-3ed2-42e2-bf89-27948c362514","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:22:40.039Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"c868826d-3950-4f0f-9ecd-4a549cdd6983","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"claude/orca-import-menu","slug":"dapper-knitting-moler"}
